206-item: every item inside it in reach (containment@1 custody: no closed or locked lid on the way),
207-at any depth, flattened in DefinitionRefString order, each with its `container_id` (its direct
208-container), its `state` if it has a barrier, and as actions only `take` and its container verbs
209-(a `ContentView`; a recursive view is not allowed in the schemas). An NPC's possessions and a
210-worn item's contents are never shown (c1-locks); `equipment`, one entry per slot
211-holder in slot-key order with its `slot` and, when one is worn, the `item` with the actions it
212-accepts (only those resolving to `remove`), absent when the world has no holder
213-([equipment@1](mechanics.md#equipment1-kerneltssrcrulesequipmentts)); `journal` (each quest the player
214-has an instance of, with state and title, and optional `journal`, the selected TextKey
215-from [quest@1](mechanics.md#quest1-rulesquestts-kerneltssrcquestts)); `chapter` (`{index, title}`, a non-negative declaration index and TextKey), present exactly
216-when the cartridge declares chapters, selected by [Chapters](mechanics.md#chapters-kerneltssrcviewts);
217-`scene` (`{scene, line, index, count}`, DefinitionRef, TextKey, one-based shown line and
218-narrate count), present exactly while [scene@1](mechanics.md#scene1-rulesscenets) runs;
219-`time` (the logical clock); the pending `choice`
220-(prompt, speaker id, closable, each option available or blocked, `kernel/ts/src/dialogue.ts:80`); and
221-`resources`, each with current, maximum, a condition band key and its tone (`normal`, `warning`
222-or `danger`, which the presenter maps to a colour) from the table in effect: the pool's own
223-`bands` (resources.json), else the cartridge's `world.bands` (cartridge.json), else the engine
224-default of 11 bands by percentage of the range, `perfect_health` at 100 down to `dying` at 0,
225-tones `normal` from 80, `warning` from 40, `danger` below (`kernel/ts/src/view.ts:216`, `:235`). The band is the
226-first row whose cut p reaches, in integers: 100 × (current − minimum) ≥ cut × (maximum −
227-minimum); maximum = minimum gives the top row (04 §15 as amended 2026-10-02).
228-Actions are listed highest priority first, then by key, available or with the refusal code
229-(`kernel/ts/src/action_lists.ts:33`). Invariant `gameview_agrees_with_admission` holds this for exits and
230-recipes, and for the door and container verbs and `wear`/`remove`, matched by the Command each
231-listed action resolves to (a cartridge alias included): one listed on its exit or item (a nested
232-one in `contents` included) is never refused with a code the view predicts (`not_present`
233-among them), one not listed is never accepted, and none of `wear`/`remove` is a place action; a
234-position invocation (`stand`, `sit`, `rest`, `sleep`) checks its selected `action_key` when
235-the observation supplies it: an available matching place action is never refused
236-`invalid_state`, and an unavailable or absent one is never accepted. Without an action key,
237-any available place action resolving to that command qualifies. An available exit's move is
238-never refused `invalid_state` or `unsupported_capability`; a
239-`take` listed on an item is never refused `not_present` (`kernel/ts/src/invariants_view.ts:29`, `:76`).

